    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "As warmer spring conditions offer a glimmer of hope for the journey, there has been a rise in crossings at the U.S. border. This led to an increase in border encounters, with data interpreters noting the shift. Year-to-date, however, crossing numbers stay historically low, as policies designed to protect national order remain in effect.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Innocent",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-0",
          "result-0"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.78
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "People seeking safety and a better life are part of an affected population at the southwest border, where public servants working to maintain order are active. Despite this seasonal change, a legislative stalemate persists in Congress. Leaders who could choose cooperation face an opportunity to find common ground on funding, but disagreement currently harms those in need.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Innocent",
